0..76 Comment "//! The terms of a sort of a theory: a fragment at two widths as one theory."
77..80 Comment "//!"
81..154 Comment "//! A fragment of a machine language has terms at more than one width. An"
155..232 Comment "//! operation takes terms at some widths and gives a term at one width, and a"
233..309 Comment "//! rule relates two terms at one width. A theory states this with a sort of"
310..370 Comment "//! the widths and a sort of the terms that a width indexes."
371..374 Comment "//!"
375..452 Comment "//! `Terms S s` is the type of the closed terms of the sort `s` of the theory"
453..528 Comment "//! `S`. Each operation into the sort is a constructor, written `S.op`. The"
529..604 Comment "//! terms of an indexed sort are a family over the terms of its index sort."
605..679 Comment "//! `Terms S s i` is the type of the terms at the index `i`. A constructor"
680..758 Comment "//! stands at the index that its operation states, and a rule of the sort is a"
759..782 Comment "//! rule of the family."
783..786 Comment "//!"
787..803 Comment "//! - see: #8358"
804..882 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/desc/terms-of-a-sort.gandr` — the sorts outside the"
883..894 Comment "//!   slice"
895..974 Comment "//! - see: `model/desc/family-with-rules.gandr` — the same family, written by"
975..985 Comment "//!   hand"
986..1067 Comment "//! - owes: #4150 — an operation or a rule across two plain sorts, and an index"
1068..1089 Comment "//!   with a variable"
